Subject: LangSOP Initial Workflow V2 Canonical Specification
Date: 2026-05-25

@ [source_manifest] docs/source/2026-05-25_langsop_initial_workflow_v2/Source_Document_Manifest.sop
@ [exploded_specification] docs/exploded/LangSOP_Initial_Workflow.v2.exploded.sop
@ [prior_canonical] docs/canonical/LangSOP_Initial_Workflow.canonical.sop
@ [prior_capability_seed] docs/planning/Capability_Field_Seed.sop
@ [sjs_protocol] platform/refinement/Specification_Justification_Solution.sop

& [CanonicalRecord: LangSOPInitialWorkflowV2] is the processed v2 planning authority for LangSOP
  + [canonical_uuid] is 6b2f499c-a572-44c4-a13a-e8c9c1ea1fa0
  + [source_manifest_uuid] is 45bf86c8-ded3-4f8a-b664-ebbc25e02747
  + [exploded_uuid] is 9d60b07e-49c3-4c40-b7bb-2cbaa8412b87
  + [authority_scope] is layer split, authority-kernel data model, LangGraph procedure model, surface projection model, fault model, and staged development frontier
  + [implementation_scope] is specification and planning authority only
  + [supersedes] is docs/canonical/LangSOP_Initial_Workflow.canonical.sop for planning details covered by v2
  + [satisfaction_signature] is [SatisfactionSignature: LangSOPInitialWorkflowV2]

  = must: treat this file as current LangSOP planning authority until superseded or invalidated
  = must: preserve v1 artifacts and v2 source snapshots as lineage
  = must: forbid runtime implementation claims from this file alone
  = must: require future solution records for implemented schemas, operators, graphs, or surfaces

& [CanonicalArchitectureContractV2] is the stable architecture split
  + [sop_semantic_layer] is source, proof, SJS authority, semantic debugging, and reconsideration
  + [authority_kernel_layer] is truth-bearing typed record storage and derived-projection governance
  + [langgraph_procedure_layer] is executable workflow over authority kernel records
  + [surface_projection_layer] is manager, worker, narrative, debug, chat, Langflow, Codex, terminal, IRC, Matrix, and web projections
  + [judgment_layer] is human or model reasoning for ambiguity, high risk, semantic conflict, and authority mutation

  = must: preserve SOP as authority and soft-wire debugging source
  = must: keep kernel records as truth-bearing runtime state
  = must: keep LangGraph checkpoints as execution state
  = must: keep surfaces as projections and validated input channels
  = must: escalate to judgment_layer when compiled operators encounter semantic uncertainty or authority conflict

& [CanonicalKernelRecordContractV2] is the initial logical data contract
  + [record_kind_set] is source_log, log_entry, citation_ref, narrative_node, understanding_anchor, capability_node, requirement_record, support_record, support_gap, authority_artifact, coordination_claim, operator_contract, operator_trace, work_packet, completion_review, readiness_projection, stale_projection, proof_result, and fault_record
  + [shared_field] is record_id
  + [shared_field] is record_kind
  + [shared_field] is natural_key
  + [shared_field] is subject_ref
  + [shared_field] is authority_state
  + [shared_field] is source_ref_set
  + [shared_field] is lineage_edge_set
  + [shared_field] is freshness_rule
  + [shared_field] is status

  = must: define natural keys before choosing physical storage
  = must: distinguish source data from derived projections
  = must: preserve source_ref_set for every claim-bearing or derived record
  = must: keep invalidated, contradicted, and stale records as trace

& [CanonicalCapabilityPlanningContractV2] is the whole-field planning contract
  + [planning_primitive] is capability_node
  + [execution_primitive] is work_packet
  + [blocked_objective] is first-class planning material
  + [readiness_projection] is derived and recomputable
  + [completion_review] is required before next packetization after completed work

  = must: bake the whole capability field before slicing work
  = must: generate work packets only from readiness, support, authority, proof, dependency, ownership, risk, and verification conditions
  = must: record blocked_reason for blocked or deferred capability nodes
  = must: recompute readiness after completion_review changes support, requirements, proof, or freshness

& [CanonicalOperatorContractV2] is the common shape for compiled SOP duties
  + [operator_id] is stable identifier
  + [source_sop_ref] is the SOP authority that justifies the operator
  + [input_record_kind_set] is required kernel record kinds
  + [output_record_kind_set] is created or updated kernel record kinds
  + [precondition_set] is required authority, freshness, and data-shape conditions
  + [postcondition_set] is guaranteed state after success
  + [interrupt_condition_set] is conditions requiring human or model judgment
  + [fault_condition_set] is conditions that emit fault_record or blocked output
  + [trace_schema] is the operator_trace shape
  + [fixture_set] is deterministic cases proving valid, invalid, stale, blocked, and ambiguous behavior

  = must: define operator contracts before LangGraph node implementation
  = must: preserve trace_schema for audit against SOP authority
  = must: return to SOP-first handling when interrupt_condition_set is active

& [CanonicalLangGraphContractV2] is the first graph execution contract
  + [graph_name] is WholeFieldPlannerGraph
  + [graph_state_role] is resumable execution state and kernel record references
  + [kernel_state_role] is truth-bearing source, authority, narrative, support, readiness, and proof state
  + [node_contract] is GraphNodeContract from v2 exploded specification
  + [required_node] is SourceIntakeNode
  + [required_node] is BoundaryDelineationNode
  + [required_node] is CapabilityFieldUpdateNode
  + [required_node] is DataIdentityNode
  + [required_node] is RequirementSupportNode
  + [required_node] is AuthorityClassificationNode
  + [required_node] is ReadinessProjectionNode
  + [required_node] is PacketizationNode
  + [required_node] is CoordinationPreflightNode
  + [required_node] is DispatchNode
  + [required_node] is CompletionReviewNode
  + [required_node] is NarrativeUpdateNode
  + [required_node] is SJSAuthorityUpdateNode

  = must: treat nodes as operators over kernel records
  = must: store meaning-bearing results outside graph checkpoint state
  = must: expose interrupts for authority conflict, ambiguous identity, missing proof route, and high-risk operation

& [CanonicalSurfaceContractV2] is the projection contract
  + [manager_surface] is capability, readiness, blocker, packet, claim, proof, and frontier view
  + [worker_surface] is bounded packet view with authority basis, preconditions, expected outputs, and verification oracle
  + [narrative_surface] is subject-tree, narrative-weave, proof, decision, dead-end, readiness, and frontier view
  + [debug_surface] is source log, operator trace, stale projection, invalidation, and fault view
  + [chat_surface] is conversation projection over source logs and narrative anchors
  + [langflow_surface] is optional visual prototype generated from operator or graph contracts

  = must: preserve source_record_set and freshness_rule for each surface projection
  = must: display authority_notice when decisions may be made from the projection
  = must: submit mutations through validated operators
  - never: let surfaces mutate canonical authority directly

& [CanonicalFaultContractV2] is the initial operational fault contract
  + [critical_fault] is checkpoint_authority_confusion
  + [critical_fault] is surface_truth_confusion
  + [critical_fault] is false_ready_packet
  + [critical_fault] is unreviewed_completion
  + [critical_fault] is over_compilation
  + [critical_fault] is unsupported_operations_control

  = must: emit fault_record for unknown, unsafe, stale, or ambiguous operator outcomes
  = must: block runtime escalation when critical faults are active
  = must: route reusable fault lessons through SOP-first reconsideration before compiling new rules

& [CanonicalDevelopmentFrontierV2] is the ordered v2 work frontier
  + [frontier_1] is kernel record schema and natural-key design
  + [frontier_2] is storage decision and source/projection preservation rules
  + [frontier_3] is operator contract template and first authority/readiness operators
  + [frontier_4] is deterministic fixture pack for capability fields, signatures, support readiness, and packetization
  + [frontier_5] is minimal LangGraph proof-of-shape using fixture kernel records
  + [frontier_6] is manager, worker, narrative, and debug surface projections over fixture records
  + [frontier_7] is first end-to-end compiled ReasoningFramework duty with SOP comparison trace
  + [frontier_8] is operations-manager safety specification before live machine control

  = must: complete frontier_1 through frontier_3 before relying on runtime graph behavior
  = must: keep frontier_8 signed before live operations-manager work
  = should: classify fixture, validator, template, and projection implementation as Spark-suitable after contracts stabilize

& [Justification: LangSOPInitialWorkflowV2] is the evidence bridge for accepting v2
  + [claim] is LangSOP is ready for schema and operator-contract design
  + [support] is preserved v1 snapshots, v2 source manifest, seven-fold exploded processing, expanded data model, graph model, authority model, surface model, fault model, and development frontier
  + [confidence] is high for layer boundaries, whole-field planning, and the rule that LangGraph is procedure rather than authority
  + [confidence] is moderate for storage backend, first operator sequence, and Langflow depth because those remain frontier decisions
  + [counterargument] is too much schema detail before implementation feedback could freeze an untested physical model
  + [invalidation_condition] is broken_source_snapshot_lineage, hidden_authority_state, checkpoint_authority_confusion, false_ready_packet, failed_schema_fixture, or implementation_contradiction

  ! [LangSOPInitialWorkflowV2AcceptedForSchemaAndOperatorDesign] is accepted
    @ [support] [CanonicalKernelRecordContractV2]
    @ [support] [CanonicalOperatorContractV2]
    @ [support] [CanonicalLangGraphContractV2]
    @ [support] [CanonicalDevelopmentFrontierV2]
    @ [support] [SatisfactionSignature: LangSOPInitialWorkflowV2]

